    <div class="cat"><span>🍽️</span> Food — slim pickings, honest options</div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Primm Valley Resort Diner</div><span class="badge b-top">MOST RELIABLE</span></div><div class="item-desc">Primm is fundamentally a border-town fuel-up — the resort diner is the best sit-down option, serving hearty breakfast plates, burgers, and comfort food 24/7. Prices are reasonable, the booths are comfortable, and the servers are experienced road-tripper wranglers. <em>Don't overthink Primm — eat here, stretch the dog, and push north.</em></div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Primm+Valley+Resort+Casino+Nevada" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Denny's at Primm</div><span class="badge b-std">24/7 RELIABLE</span></div><div class="item-desc">Open 24 hours, no surprises, and the Strawberry Stuffed French Toast Slam is genuinely good according to the local who wrote about it. One reviewer called it one of the better-run Denny's they'd visited. Fine for a quick, reliable stop before Vegas.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Denny%27s+Primm+Nevada" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🐾</span> Dog Walk</div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Primm Valley Desert Stretch</div></div><div class="item-desc">The open desert scrubland around the resort parking lots is walkable and leash-friendly — not a park, but wide open space and surprisingly quiet once you get away from the main road. Walk toward the sand hills behind the casino complex. Brief but effective. Clean restrooms in the casino. <em>This stretch is legitimately beautiful desert at golden hour.</em></div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Primm+Nevada" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
