  <div class="town-body">
    <div class="cs"><div class="cs-l"><div class="cs-ico">⚡</div><div><div class="cs-title">Tesla Supercharger — Richfield, UT</div><div class="cs-detail">Near downtown Richfield · I-70 / I-15 junction · Confirmed active 24/7 · Great overnight charging town</div></div></div><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Tesla+Supercharger+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🍽️</span> Food</div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Severo</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 BEST IN RICHFIELD</span></div><div class="item-desc">By a wide margin the most praised restaurant in Richfield — reviewers describe it as one of the best meals they've had on any road trip, ever. <em>"Chimichurri steak mac and cheese, cast iron cornbread, shepherd's pie, Utah filet, Annabella chicken"</em> — a rotating farm-to-table menu in a Western-themed space with intimate lighting and exceptional service. A genuine destination restaurant in a surprising location.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Severo+Restaurant+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.8 · Best surprise of the route</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Borens Smokehouse</div><span class="badge b-std">BEST BBQ</span></div><div class="item-desc">Central Utah BBQ institution — <em>"wow, not what I was expecting when I randomly had to stay in Richfield UT... I might've had the best BBQ."</em> The Boren burger and mac and cheese squares are standouts. One of those places you'd walk past a thousand times and then be astounded.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Borens+Smokehouse+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.6</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Little Wonder Cafe</div><span class="badge b-std">100+ YEAR INSTITUTION</span></div><div class="item-desc">Standing on Main Street for over 100 years — a genuine piece of Utah road history. Local food guide calls it one of their favorites. The kind of small-town cafe that defines the I-70 character of central Utah. Great for a quick, honest meal.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Little+Wonder+Cafe+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.3</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Steve's Steakhouse</div><span class="badge b-std">EVENING OPTION · OPENS 4PM</span></div><div class="item-desc">Perfectly cooked steaks and crisp salads — reviewers who arrived after a long day on the road call it the high point of the trip. The server Veronica has her own fan club in the review section. Opens at 4pm, ideal for an early dinner if you're overnighting in Richfield.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Steve%27s+Steakhouse+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.4 · Dinner only from 4pm</span></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🐾</span> Dog Walk</div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Richfield City Park</div></div><div class="item-desc">Grassy, shaded city park right downtown near the Supercharger — a clean, pleasant stretch for the dog between sessions. BringFido specifically lists the Richfield Visitor Center as a dog-friendly stop here. Combine the walk with your charger stop. <em>Elevation ~5,300 ft — cool and breezy, a great contrast to the lower desert.</em></div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Richfield+City+Park+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Fishlake National Forest Trailheads</div><span class="badge b-std">20–30 MIN WEST · SPECTACULAR</span></div><div class="item-desc">If you have extra time — Fishlake National Forest is a 20-min drive west of Richfield and offers dog-friendly trails through aspen groves and high mountain terrain around Fish Lake itself. Leashed dogs welcome on most trails. One of Utah's most underrated landscapes and a complete change from the desert.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Fish+Lake+Utah+National+Forest" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🏨</span> Hotels</div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Hampton Inn Richfield</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 TOP PICK</span></div><div class="item-desc">The best-reviewed full-service hotel in Richfield — free hot breakfast, clean rooms, great water pressure, friendly staff. BringFido confirms up to 75 lb limit ($20/night pet fee). Easy I-70/I-15 access. Consistently excellent reviews from road-trippers who planned to just pass through and ended up happy they stayed.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Hampton+Inn+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 8.9/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Up to 75 lb · $20/night</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Fairfield Inn &amp; Suites Richfield</div><span class="badge b-std">RELIABLE MARRIOTT</span></div><div class="item-desc">Modern Marriott property — any size dogs welcome (2 pets max), $50 flat stay fee. Breakfast included, clean and consistent. <em>"BW Richfield — plenty of room to walk the dog"</em> note on the adjacent Best Western applies to this block too. Good infrastructure for a pet-traveling family.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Fairfield+Inn+Suites+Richfield+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Any size · $50 flat fee</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Comfort Inn Richfield I-70</div><span class="badge b-std">VALUE OPTION</span></div><div class="item-desc">Well-reviewed I-70 roadside Comfort Inn — dog-friendly rooms with grassy relief areas and poop bags on site. Treats at the front desk. Consistent guest satisfaction ratings, fast access to Severo for dinner. A solid budget-friendly choice.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Comfort+Inn+Richfield+I-70+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Up to 35 lb · $20/night · Treats at desk</span></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

