    <div class="cat"><span>☕🍽️</span> Coffee + Lunch — best charger combo stop of the entire route</div>
    <div class="item coffee"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Green River Coffee Co.</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 EV ROAD TRIPPER #1</span></div><div class="item-desc">EV road-trippers call this their single favorite charging stop on the entire US Tesla network. In-house fair-trade roasted coffee, legendary breakfast burritos (~$10, enormous), and an authentically eclectic space — giant red velvet couch reportedly from a brothel in Helper, UT, art everywhere, a reading room. Owner Amy has been running this since 2004. <em>This is a highlight of the trip regardless of whether you need coffee.</em></div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Green+River+Coffee+Co+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.9 · EV travelers' #1</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Ray's Tavern</div><span class="badge b-std">I-70 LEGEND</span></div><div class="item-desc">Crowned "best pit stop on I-70" by Salt Lake Magazine. Classic bar burgers, cold beer, no-nonsense atmosphere. A genuine roadside institution since the 1960s. Cash-preferred, character-rich. Go if you want a cold beer and a real burger in a place that's been unchanged for decades.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Ray%27s+Tavern+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.3 · Cash preferred</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Tamarisk Restaurant</div><span class="badge b-std">ACROSS FROM CHARGER</span></div><div class="item-desc">Classic American diner directly across the street from the Supercharger — burgers, sandwiches, river views through the windows. The most convenient sit-down option if Green River Coffee is packed. Reliable and well-positioned.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Tamarisk+Restaurant+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.0 · Steps from charger</span></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🐾</span> Dog Walk</div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Green River State Park — Riverbank Trail</div><span class="badge b-top">COMBINE WITH CHARGE STOP</span></div><div class="item-desc">Short drive from the Supercharger — leashed dogs welcome on scenic trails along the Green River under giant cottonwood trees. The canyon walls above are spectacular, the river is calm and beautiful, and <em>dogs can wade in calmer bank areas</em>. Plan 30–45 minutes here alongside your coffee and lunch stop. One of the finest mid-drive dog walks on the route.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Green+River+State+Park+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Crystal Geyser Road — River Road Walk</div><span class="badge b-std">UNIQUE GEOLOGICAL CURIOSITY</span></div><div class="item-desc">Drive south on River Road to the Crystal Geyser — a natural CO2 cold-water geyser that erupts on a rough schedule. Dogs welcome in the open desert landscape. The road itself winds alongside the Green River through beautiful canyon scenery. Best if you have an extra 30+ minutes.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Crystal+Geyser+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🏨</span> Hotels</div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">First Choice Inn at the Swell</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 TOP PICK</span></div><div class="item-desc">Reviewers gush: <em>"clean big rooms, pet-friendly, indoor pool and jacuzzi"</em> — <em>"lovely green space and dog-friendly grounds"</em> — <em>"good price, perfect halfway location, amazing hospitality."</em> Indoor pool, full hot breakfast, and genuinely excellent dog accommodations. The best hotel in Green River for pet-traveling road-trippers.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=First+Choice+Inn+at+the+Swell+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 8.2/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Dog grounds on site</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Holiday Inn Express Green River</div><span class="badge b-std">CONSISTENT</span></div><div class="item-desc">Standard Holiday Inn Express — comfortable beds, free breakfast, easy I-70 access. Reliable and uncomplicated. Lets you get on the road early. Pets allowed with fee.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Holiday+Inn+Express+Green+River+Utah" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Pets with fee</span></div></div>
