    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Battlement Mesa Grill &amp; Local Spots</div><span class="badge b-top">LOCAL CHARACTER</span></div><div class="item-desc">Parachute is a small oil-country town at the confluence of Parachute Creek and the Colorado River — a handful of local restaurants and diners serve the ranching and energy community. The town has a genuine frontier feel without tourist inflation. Colorado.com calls the food range "a nice variety for a quick pull-off." <em>Ask locals at the gas station next to the Supercharger what's open and good — that intel is always current.</em></div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Parachute+Colorado+restaurants" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🐾</span> Dog Walk</div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Colorado River Access — Parachute Creek Confluence</div><span class="badge b-top">BEAUTIFUL RIVER WALK</span></div><div class="item-desc">The town sits at the meeting of Parachute Creek and the Colorado River — there are informal river-access points with flat, easy walking along both waterways. Leash required, but the setting is genuinely lovely: big cottonwoods, the sound of the river, and views of the Book Cliffs to the north. <em>Dogs can wade in the river in calmer stretches.</em> A hidden gem of a charge-stop walk.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Parachute+Creek+Colorado+River+confluence+Parachute+CO" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
