  </button>
  <div class="town-body">
    <div class="cs"><div class="cs-l"><div class="cs-ico">⚡</div><div><div class="cs-title">Tesla Supercharger — Glenwood Springs</div><div class="cs-detail">125 Wulfsohn Rd · 6 stalls · 24/7 · Courtyard Marriott is directly across the street · Near Glenwood mall with Target and Petco</div></div></div><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Tesla+Supercharger+125+Wulfsohn+Road+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>☕</span> Coffee</div>
    <div class="item coffee"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Sweet Coloradough Bakery &amp; Café</div><span class="badge b-top">LOCAL MORNING SPOT</span></div><div class="item-desc">Downtown bakery with fresh-baked goods, excellent coffee, sandwiches, and soups. Beloved by locals as the go-to morning stop. Perfect for grabbing road pastries and a proper latte before the final mountain drive. Walk in directly from Hotel Colorado.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Sweet+Coloradough+Bakery+Cafe+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.8</span></div></div>
    <div class="item coffee"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Riverblend Coffee House</div><span class="badge b-std">DOG-FRIENDLY PATIO</span></div><div class="item-desc">Riverside coffee house with a dog-friendly patio along the Colorado River. Specifically recommended in Glenwood's official pet-friendly guide for travelers with dogs. A lovely place to sit with your dog and watch the river before hitting I-70.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Riverblend+Coffee+House+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.5</span></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🍽️</span> Food</div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">The Pullman</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 BEST IN GLENWOOD</span></div><div class="item-desc">Top-rated restaurant in Glenwood Springs — locally sourced ranch beef, sustainable salmon, Rocky Mountain trout, craft cocktails with Colorado spirits. The 14-oz cowboy cut ribeye and lobster ravioli are the standouts. On Restaurant Row, steps from Hotel Colorado.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=The+Pullman+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.7</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Glenwood Canyon Brewpub</div><span class="badge b-std">CANYON VIEWS + CRAFT BEER</span></div><div class="item-desc">Lively local brewpub in a canyon-view setting — excellent craft beer and a solid pub menu. The truffle risotto and house brews are consistently praised. A great casual evening after a long driving day.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Glenwood+Canyon+Brewpub+Glenwood+Springs" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.4</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">19th Street Diner</div><span class="badge b-std">FUNKY 50s CLASSIC</span></div><div class="item-desc">World-famous meatloaf, smoked pulled pork, pot roast, and hearty comfort food in a gloriously eccentric 1950s setting. Funky, fun, and genuinely loved. Perfect if you want something unforgettable and unpretentious.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=19th+Street+Diner+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 4.0 · A local legend</span></div></div>
    <div class="item food"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Sundae Artisan Ice Cream</div><span class="badge b-std">🍦 MUST-DO DESSERT</span></div><div class="item-desc">Small-batch artisan ice cream in creative flavors, served in handmade waffle cones. Recognized by Travel + Leisure. Right on Restaurant Row — the natural after-dinner walk. The perfect Colorado treat before crashing.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Sundae+Artisan+Ice+Cream+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 4.8 · Don't skip this</span></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🐾</span> Dog Walk — outstanding options</div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Two Rivers Park + Rio Grande Trail</div><span class="badge b-top">BEST DOG WALK ON THE ROUTE</span></div><div class="item-desc">At the confluence of the Colorado and Roaring Fork Rivers — grassy fields, picnic tables, and a <em>fenced off-leash area</em> for dogs under voice control. The adjacent Rio Grande Trail is paved and runs all the way toward Aspen. <em>River bank areas where dogs can wade.</em> Visit Glenwood's pet guide calls this the crown jewel of the city's dog-friendly spots. Plan 30–45 minutes here.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Two+Rivers+Park+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Glenwood Canyon Recreation Path</div><span class="badge b-std">SPECTACULAR PAVED PATH</span></div><div class="item-desc">Paved path through the bottom of Glenwood Canyon alongside the Colorado River — leashed dogs welcome. Views of sheer canyon walls are extraordinary. Several I-70 trailheads (No Name, Grizzly Creek). Do as much or as little as you want. One of the most spectacular easy dog walks in Colorado.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Glenwood+Canyon+Recreation+Path+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="item dog"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Glenwood Springs Dog Park</div><span class="badge b-std">FENCED OFF-LEASH</span></div><div class="item-desc">Dedicated fenced off-leash park along the Rio Grande Trail south of Glenwood Springs High School — playground equipment for dogs, fetch and frisbee space. Glenwood's official go-to for off-leash play.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Glenwood+Springs+Dog+Park+Rio+Grande+Trail" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a></div></div>
    <div class="cat"><span>🏨</span> Hotels</div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Hotel Colorado</div><span class="badge b-top">🏆 MOST CHARACTER + PET AMENITIES</span></div><div class="item-desc">Historic 1893 landmark on the Colorado River — rated 9.0/10. Provides food and water bowls for pet guests. Beautiful courtyard dining. Steps from Two Rivers Park and Restaurant Row. Teddy Roosevelt once stayed here. The most memorable overnight of the entire route.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Hotel+Colorado+526+Pine+St+Glenwood+Springs" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 9.0/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Bowls provided</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Courtyard by Marriott Glenwood Springs</div><span class="badge b-std">DIRECTLY ACROSS FROM SUPERCHARGER</span></div><div class="item-desc">The most practical Tesla road-tripper choice — directly across the street from the Supercharger at 125 Wulfsohn Rd. Top off overnight while you sleep. Heated outdoor pool, reliable Marriott quality, easy I-70 departure.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Courtyard+Marriott+Glenwood+Springs+125+Wulfsohn+Road" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 8.5/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Supercharger across the street</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Hotel Maxwell Anderson</div><span class="badge b-std">BOUTIQUE DESIGN</span></div><div class="item-desc">Stylish boutique hotel with distinctive design, mountain views, and a central downtown location. One of Booking.com's most popular pet-friendly picks in Glenwood. Highly reviewed for service and atmosphere.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Hotel+Maxwell+Anderson+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 8.9/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Pet-friendly</span></div></div>
    <div class="item hotel"><div class="item-top"><div class="item-name">Hampton Inn Glenwood Springs</div><span class="badge b-std">CONSISTENT VALUE</span></div><div class="item-desc">Free hot breakfast, indoor pool, mountain views. Reliable and clean. A comfortable, no-surprises option at a lower price than the boutique hotels. Easy I-70 access for an early departure.</div><div class="item-meta"><a class="map-btn" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Hampton+Inn+Glenwood+Springs+Colorado" target="_blank">📍 Maps</a><span class="rating"><span class="stars">★★★★</span> 8.4/10</span><span class="pet-pill">🐾 Pet-friendly</span></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

